IMPORT prelude

-- Foreign Employee Dormitories Act 2015 (Singapore) -- who is a foreign employee and which premises are a foreign employee
-- dormitory (ss 2, 3), the licence requirement and its offences (s 7), licence term and renewal (s 10), the Commissioner's
-- directives and regulatory action as they reach residents (ss 12-15), stopping operation (s 20), questioning and arrest
-- (ss 24-26), and composition (s 28).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FEDA2015.txt. The deposit
-- says the revised edition incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021, and each page is headed "Informal Consolidation --
-- version in force from 1/12/2025". The latest amendment annotated is Act 31 of 2023 (Immigration (Amendment) Act 2023), which
-- touches the definitions of "foreigner" (wef 31/12/2024) and "permanent resident of Singapore" (wef 01/12/2025) in s 2(1).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it governs the large dormitories where many foreign workers in Singapore
-- live, and what the State may order their operators to do (including restricting residents' movement, s 13(4)(d)). SCOPED to the
-- provisions a resident, an operator or a proprietor most often meets. Not encoded: application contents and inspection on
-- application (s 8), the grounds the Commissioner weighs (s 9(2)), licence conditions and their penalty (s 11), disqualification
-- (s 16), transfer (s 17), annual returns (s 18), codes of practice (s 19), the Register (s 21), appeals
-- (ss 22-23), entry and search powers beyond questioning (s 24(1)-(5)), liability of officers (s 27), and service (s 30). No regulations, codes of practice or Gazette notifications were retrieved, so the "threshold
-- number", the "prescribed occupancy load" and which offences are compoundable are inputs, not facts.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Foreign Employee Dormitories Act 2015`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `2(1) -- foreign employee`

-- s 2(1): "foreigner" means an individual who is neither a citizen of Singapore nor a permanent resident of Singapore.
-- "foreign employee" means a foreigner -- (a) "who seeks employment, or is employed to work, in Singapore but excludes a
-- self-employed foreigner"; or (b) "whose employment in Singapore has expired or has been terminated (whether or not for
-- justified reasons) and is authorised under the Immigration Act 1959 to remain in Singapore".
-- The self-employed exclusion sits in paragraph (a) only; it is read here as not qualifying paragraph (b).
GIVEN `a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN, `seeks or is in employment in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN, `employment ended but authorised to remain` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is a foreign employee` IF
        (NOT `a citizen`)
    AND (NOT `a permanent resident`)
    AND (    (`seeks or is in employment in Singapore` AND (NOT `self-employed`))
         OR  `employment ended but authorised to remain`)

§§ `3 -- foreign employee dormitory`

-- s 3(1): "foreign employee dormitory" means any boarding premises that -- (a) provide the threshold number of beds or higher for use
-- by residents who are foreign employees; (b) provide accommodation to the threshold number of residents who are foreign employees,
-- or higher; or (c) have the prescribed occupancy load and provide accommodation substantially to foreign employees.
-- (2): the Act does NOT apply to hotels, inns, hostels, B&Bs; serviced apartments; aged-care, nursing and convalescent homes;
-- student hostels; "a house"; "a self-contained residence that is a flat or an apartment"; prisons and detention places; work
-- vessels; government crisis accommodation; and premises excluded by Ministerial order.
-- (3): "threshold number" means 1,000 or any lower number that the Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, prescribe.
DECLARE PremisesKind IS ONE OF
    `boarding premises of no excluded kind`
    `a hotel, inn, hostel or B&B`
    `a serviced apartment`
    `a nursing or convalescent home`
    `a student hostel`
    `a house`
    `a flat or apartment`
    `a prison or detention place`
    `a vessel housing its crew`
    `government crisis accommodation`
    `premises excluded by Ministerial order`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the statutory threshold number` MEANS 1000

GIVEN `the kind` IS A PremisesKind, `beds for foreign employees` IS A NUMBER, `foreign employee residents` IS A NUMBER,
      `the threshold in force` IS A NUMBER, `has the prescribed occupancy load` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `houses substantially foreign employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises are a foreign employee dormitory` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `boarding premises of no excluded kind` THEN
            `beds for foreign employees` AT LEAST `the threshold in force`
        OR  `foreign employee residents` AT LEAST `the threshold in force`
        OR  (`has the prescribed occupancy load` AND `houses substantially foreign employees`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7 -- licence needed`

-- s 7(1): unless exempted under s 32, a person must not operate boarding premises as a foreign employee dormitory except under a
-- valid licence. (2): a proprietor must not use or permit the use of premises as a foreign employee dormitory unless used as such by
-- a licensed operator. (3): fine up to $500,000 or imprisonment up to 2 years or both; on a second or subsequent conviction, up to
-- $1 million or 4 years or both. (4): defence for the PROPRIETOR (s 7(2) only) who proves on a balance of probabilities that it "did
-- not know, and could not reasonably have been expected to know". (5): arrestable.
GIVEN `exempted under section 32` IS A BOOLEAN, `operates a foreign employee dormitory` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds a valid licence for the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator commits the s 7(1) offence` IF
    (NOT `exempted under section 32`) AND `operates a foreign employee dormitory` AND (NOT `holds a valid licence for the premises`)

GIVEN `exempted under section 32` IS A BOOLEAN, `premises used as a foreign employee dormitory` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `used by a licensed operator` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved it did not and could not reasonably know` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proprietor is guilty under s 7(2)` IF
        (NOT `exempted under section 32`)
    AND `premises used as a foreign employee dormitory`
    AND (NOT `used by a licensed operator`)
    AND (NOT `proved it did not and could not reasonably know`)

GIVEN `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlicensed operation` MEANS
    IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 1000000 ELSE 500000

GIVEN `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years for unlicensed operation` MEANS
    IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 4 ELSE 2

§§ `10 -- licence term and renewal`

-- s 10(2): a licence continues in force for the period specified in it "(not exceeding 3 years)". (4): a renewal application "must be
-- made no later than 3 months before the date of expiry ... unless otherwise allowed by the Commissioner in any particular case, which
-- is to be treated as a late renewal application". Read here: a later application can be entertained only if the Commissioner allows
-- it, and is then a late renewal application. The "longer period that may be prescribed in substitution" is not modelled.
GIVEN `years specified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence term is within s 10(2)` IF
    `years specified` GREATER THAN 0 AND `years specified` AT MOST 3

GIVEN `months before expiry` IS A NUMBER, `the Commissioner allows it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the renewal application may be considered` IF
    `months before expiry` AT LEAST 3 OR `the Commissioner allows it`

GIVEN `months before expiry` IS A NUMBER, `the Commissioner allows it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a late renewal application` IF
    `months before expiry` LESS THAN 3 AND `the Commissioner allows it`

§§ `12 -- modifying licence conditions`

-- s 12(2)(b): before modifying conditions, notice giving "at least 14 days from the date of service" for written representations,
-- unless (5) applies: danger to "the security and good order" within the dormitory or "the safety and health of the residents", when
-- the Commissioner may modify "with immediate effect". (6): the operator may apply for review "within 7 days". (8): the review does
-- not suspend the decision.
GIVEN `days allowed for representations` IS A NUMBER, `danger to order or to residents' safety and health` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the modification notice is sufficient` IF
    `danger to order or to residents' safety and health` OR `days allowed for representations` AT LEAST 14

GIVEN `days after the immediate modification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the review application is in time` IF
    `days after the immediate modification` AT MOST 7

§§ `13 -- compliance directives`

-- s 13(4)(c): a directive may order the premises to stop being used as a foreign employee dormitory "for a period not exceeding
-- 3 months in order to deal with a serious and imminent threat or risk to the safety and health of the residents".
-- (4)(d): where (1)(c) applies -- a serious and imminent threat to residents' safety and health, or civil unrest, hostilities, war,
-- an election or other event that "may occasion disorder" -- it may order the operator "to check or control the movement of
-- residents ..., including restricting entry to and exit from those premises".
-- (6): breach without reasonable excuse -- fine up to $50,000 or 12 months or both "and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- further fine not exceeding $10,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
-- (7): an operator told to demolish, renovate or alter may, "within 7 days after receiving the directive", give a statutory
-- declaration that its arrangements with the proprietor prevent it. (9): no right to be heard before a directive.
GIVEN `months of stoppage` IS A NUMBER, `serious and imminent threat to residents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stoppage order is within s 13(4)(c)` IF
    `serious and imminent threat to residents` AND `months of stoppage` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months of stoppage` AT MOST 3

GIVEN `serious and imminent threat to residents` IS A BOOLEAN, `an event that may occasion disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `residents' movement may be restricted` IF
    `serious and imminent threat to residents` OR `an event that may occasion disorder`

GIVEN `days or part days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for breaching a compliance directive` MEANS
    50000 PLUS 10000 TIMES `days or part days continuing after conviction`

GIVEN `days after receiving the directive` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statutory declaration is in time` IF
    `days after receiving the directive` AT MOST 7

§§ `14 -- suspension and revocation`

-- s 14(2)(b)(vi): suspension "for not more than 6 months". (3)(c): written notice of intended action giving "at least 14 days after the
-- date of service" for representations. (2)(b)(iii): a business restriction directive is one of the lesser actions.
GIVEN `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension is within s 14` IF
    `months of suspension` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months of suspension` AT MOST 6

GIVEN `days allowed for representations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulatory action notice is sufficient` IF
    `days allowed for representations` AT LEAST 14

§§ `15 -- business restriction directives`

-- s 15(1): the directive may bar (a) occupancy agreements for a new resident; (b) entering, renewing or extending one that lets a
-- resident continue. (2): "Any purported entry, renewal or extension of an occupancy agreement in contravention of a business
-- restriction directive is void and of no effect." (3): fine up to $50,000 or 12 months or both.
GIVEN `the directive bars new residents' agreements` IS A BOOLEAN, `the directive bars renewals and extensions` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the agreement is for a new resident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupancy agreement is void` IF
        (`the directive bars new residents' agreements` AND `the agreement is for a new resident`)
    OR  (`the directive bars renewals and extensions` AND (NOT `the agreement is for a new resident`))

§§ `20 -- stopping operation`

-- s 20(1): an operator must not, without prior approval, wholly and permanently cease operating or surrender the licence. (2): the
-- application "must be made ... at least 28 days" before the cessation or surrender date. (3): conditions may include "directing the
-- licensed operator to provide assistance to foreign employees who are residents ... to find alternative accommodation in
-- Singapore". (5): ceasing without approval -- up to $200,000 or 2 years or both. (6): breaching a condition -- up to $20,000 or
-- 2 years or both.
GIVEN `days before the cessation date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cessation application is in time` IF
    `days before the cessation date` AT LEAST 28

GIVEN `ceased or surrendered` IS A BOOLEAN, `had prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator commits the s 20(5) offence` IF
    `ceased or surrendered` AND (NOT `had prior approval`)

§§ `24, 25 -- questioning and arrest`

-- s 24(6): a person asked under (1)(g) or (h) "is bound to state truly what the person knows ... except that the person need not say
-- anything that might expose that person to a criminal charge, penalty or forfeiture". (7): the statement must be written down, read
-- over, interpreted if the person "does not understand English", and signed.
-- s 25(4): a dormitory inspector must not detain an arrested individual longer than is reasonable, "and the period must not in any
-- case exceed 48 hours exclusive of the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the Magistrate's Court".
GIVEN `the answer might expose the person to a charge, penalty or forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must answer` IF
    NOT `the answer might expose the person to a charge, penalty or forfeiture`

GIVEN `hours in custody` IS A NUMBER, `hours of the journey to court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the detention is within the 48-hour limit` IF
    `hours in custody` MINUS `hours of the journey to court` AT MOST 48

§§ `26 -- false information and obstruction`

-- s 26(1): an offence to give the Commissioner or an inspector a document, statement or information that is false or misleading
-- (or misleading by omission), knowing or where the person "ought reasonably to know", in connection with (i) a licence or renewal
-- application, (ii) a representation under s 13 or 14, or (iii) an inspector's question or requirement under s 24(1) or (2) --
-- $20,000 or 2 years or both. (2): not if it is not false or misleading "in a material particular".
-- (3): obstruction -- $10,000 or 12 months or both. (4): it is NOT an offence to refuse a request of an inspector "who fails to
-- declare his or her office and refuses to produce his or her identification card on demand".
GIVEN `false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or ought reasonably to know` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `given in an application, representation or answer to an inspector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the false information offence is made out` IF
    `false or misleading in a material particular` AND `knew or ought reasonably to know`
    AND `given in an application, representation or answer to an inspector`

GIVEN `refused or obstructed` IS A BOOLEAN, `demanded the inspector's identification` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the inspector declared office or produced the card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the obstruction offence may be made out` IF
    `refused or obstructed`
    AND (NOT (`demanded the inspector's identification` AND (NOT `the inspector declared office or produced the card`)))

§§ `28 -- composition`

-- s 28(1): the Commissioner may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower
-- of" (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence"; (b) $5,000.
GIVEN `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
